## Why This Is Asked
This question introduces a new DP angle: exact k segments, per-segment cost, and sum-based values, requiring both interval DP and reconstruction.

## Key Concepts
- Prefix sums for O(1) subarray sums
- DP over i (prefix length) and t (blocks)
- Reconstructing endpoints from choice pointers

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxSumPartition(A,k,c){
  const n=A.length;
  const P=[0];
  for(const x of A) P.push(P[P.length-1]+x);
  const dp=Array.from({length:n+1},()=>Array(k+1).fill(-1e15));
  const pos=Array.from({length:n+1},()=>Array(k+1).fill(-1));
  for(let i=1;i<=n;i++) dp[i][1]=(P[i]-P[0])-c, pos[i][1]=0;
  for(let t=2;t<=k;t++){
    for(let i=t;i<=n;i++){
      for(let s=t-1;s<=i-1;s++){
        const val=dp[s][t-1]+(P[i]-P[s])-c;
        if(val>dp[i][t]){ dp[i][t]=val; pos[i][t]=s; }
      }
    }
  }
  // reconstruct
  let i=n, t=k;
  const blocks=[];
  while(t>0){
    const s=pos[i][t];
    blocks.push([s, i-1]);
    i=s; t--;
  }
  blocks.reverse();
  return {score: dp[n][k], blocks};
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Tests the ability to design a DP with two choices per step (1- or 2-length blocks), plus reconstruction and complexity awareness.

## Key Concepts

- DP with two dimensions (i, t)
- Transitions for 1-length and 2-length blocks
- Reconstruction via parent pointers
- Time/space trade-offs and potential optimization

## Code Example

```javascript
function maxValueBlocks(A, k){
  const n = A.length;
  const NEG = -1e15;
  const dp = Array.from({length: n+1}, ()=> Array(k+1).fill(NEG));
  const take = Array.from({length: n+1}, ()=> Array(k+1).fill(0));
  dp[0][0] = 0;
  for(let i=1;i<=n;i++){
    for(let t=1;t<=k;t++){
      // 1-length block ending at i-1
      if(dp[i-1][t-1] !== NEG){
        const val = dp[i-1][t-1] + A[i-1];
        if(val > dp[i][t]){ dp[i][t] = val; take[i][t] = 1; }
      }
      // 2-length block ending at i-1
      if(i>=2 && dp[i-2][t-1] !== NEG){
        const val = dp[i-2][t-1] + A[i-2] + A[i-1];
        if(val > dp[i][t]){ dp[i][t] = val; take[i][t] = 2; }
      }
    }
  }
  // reconstruction would trace back from (n, k)
  return dp[n][k];
}
```

